WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.567
-I always forget
how short I am

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.767
until I come to your show.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.467
-Nah! You know
how to do it perfect.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.200
-I'm going to totally...
Yeah, I'm going to sit.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.801
-First of all,
by the way, look at this vinyl.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.300
-I love it. Yeah.
This is one of the colors.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.601
We have so many
different colors.

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:13.634
I'm obsessed with vinyl.
It's beautiful.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.868
-I have too much.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:17.000
But yeah, I didn't like
several different colors.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.234
-You have vinyl when I did
your show

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:21.334
when it was in Los Angeles.
-Yes.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.267
-And you had a record player
in your dressing room.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.133
-Yes, I have them everywhere.
-Do you still have it with you?

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.734
-Yes, I have them everywhere.
-You're our neighbor now.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:29.033
You're right across the hall.
I know, rough commute today.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.534
-Yeah. Welcome.
-Yeah. I love it.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.133
But I forgot, I was telling
you backstage.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.133
Like I forget,
like, when my show ends

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.534
and I'm going home,
like, your show is beginning.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.334
And so I'm running into people
in the hallway and I'm like,

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.567
"This is -- I'm not this cool,
but I feel cool." [ Chuckles ]

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.834
-Because, you know, everybody.
You're like, "Yeah, what's up?"

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:43.868
-I know, you run into people,
and I'm like,

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.067
"Oh, that's awesome."

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.567
-Did you have a great
first -- first week here?

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:48.934
-I did, we --

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.467
Well, I will say
my very first day, um...

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.834
[ Chuckles ]

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.434
I -- Look, I was very tired,
and we were working a lot,

00:00:55.434 --> 00:01:00.200
and I had -- I had gotten
a venti matcha iced tea latte

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.534
and then I was just tired.

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.367
I don't know what happened,
but I got on,

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.100
it was F4,
the elevator, F4.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.567
-That was classic.
-And I -- Yeah.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.334
It is a -- It is a --
It is one of the most iconic

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:10.334
elevators
ever isn't it?

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.868
-Fallon 4.
-That's so funny.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.033
-Yeah.
-Um...

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.300
And then I proceeded
to not only drop my drink

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.868
in the entire -- Like,
I mean a full venti.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.601
And then it looked like art.
It looked like it went.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.000
It went, like, all over.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.267
-And then I knew
there were cameras.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.934
So I was like, I was like,
"Oh, my God,

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.968
this is going to be seen
my first time here."

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.934
Anyway, I have completely
trashed an elevator.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.267
That was my first -- you --

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.934
you now have a rock star
in the building, so.

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.467
-Oh, yeah.
Yeah. You trashed.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.534
-By the way...

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:36.767
-Trashed the elevator
on my way in.

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.133
-You really did. Look at this.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.567
-Yeah, no. And you...
-You really did.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.534
-You're not even...
-I've never seen that.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.300
-You're not even getting
the full spectrum.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.467
It went to the ceiling.
-Did you throw it?

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.901
Did you slam it down?
-No!

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.501
I was standing there and it
just slipped out of my hands.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:49.534
And I was like,
"What the...?"

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.100
And it went --
It went everywhere.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.634
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.067
-That's a great way to..
-You're welcome "30 Rock."

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.434
Thank you for having me.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:57.901
-I'm sure I'll be --

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.667
I'll be asking you
for favors like "Kelly.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:00.868
Please come over whenever."
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:01.968
You know I love games.
-Come sing a song.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.234
-Yeah I will sing.
I will do anything.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.400
-Yeah.
-Tap dance. Whatever.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.901
-Is there a song,
by the way, that you've sang

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.367
more than any other song
besides your own songs?

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:10.834
-Um, probably Aretha maybe.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.200
I don't know. I've sang a lot --
A lot of songs.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.868
But probably
"Never Loved a Man"

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.334
by Aretha Franklin.
-Oh, really?

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.000
Was that the song you would
sing, like, when you were a kid

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.601
like trying out
and going to talent shows?

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.367
-Oh, no. Like my very first --
I did do stuff from Aretha,

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:26.367
but my very first song, I ever,
which was a bold song to pick.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.868
I would love to say
I was brave and bold.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:31.467
I was just stupid.
But I picked "Vision of Love."

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.934
[ Chuckles ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.234
-Yeah.
-Mariah Carey.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:37.067
-I was feeling very good
about it and it went well.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.767
It went fine.
But like, I just --

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:40.934
Why would you pick that song
as your first song

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.267
to sing in front of people?
I don't know.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:43.868
-Because you like,
maybe you like the pressure.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.567
-I just love the song.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.801
-Did you ever tell Mariah
that that was your song?

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.000
-No. Oh, my God.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.000
So what -- [ Chuckles ]
I did, I did talk to her

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.234
because I was like, "Oh, I" --
She knows I adore her.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.567
Because I've run into her
several times

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:56.133
and she's probably got me
on some security list

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:58.000
to, like,
keep me away, but...

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.167
-Are you in The Lamb--
Are you a lamb?

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.501
Are you in The Lambily?
-I'm a lamb.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.734
I love her.
I love her, yes.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.601
But I --
[ Inhales sharply ]

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.434
I did something stupid.
She came on "The Voice."

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:06.934
And we were working together,
and I just --

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.968
Sometimes I say everything
that's in my brain,

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.200
and I shouldn't do that.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.033
But I was trying to say
because she was like,

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.234
"Oh, yeah,
like you're writing, too."

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.200
I was like, "Oh, my God,
I know all your songs."

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.567
Like, I'm a huge fan of her.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.234
People don't realize
she wrote all of that.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.868
Like not just sang it,
like, she wrote everything.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.100
And she was like, "Well,
we should write together."

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.868
And then in my head,
I was just like,

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.267
"Oh, yeah,
I don't really write like.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.200
I can't be, like, that
vulnerable, like, in a room.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.667
I usually just like,
write on my own."

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.267
And then I walked away and my,
my friends were like,

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:33.000
"Do you, do you realize
you just told Mariah Carey no?"

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.767
-Mariah Carey wants to write
a song with you,

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.367
and you were like,
"That's not what it meant."

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.467
-That's not what I meant.
I meant I'm not the best.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:42.400
Writing for me does not
come out in that scenario.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.634
I'm usually alone.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.868
Anytime you see my name
on a song, I wrote it.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.167
Usually alone.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.400
Yeah,but you would love to write
a song with Mariah Carey?

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.501
-I would love to write.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:52.467
I love you, Mariah Carey,
and I will --

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:55.434
I will risk it for you.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.567
But I just also
saw you recently.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.000
You made some headlines
because you

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.467
rewrote the lyrics to...
-Oh, "Piece by Piece."

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.767
-"Piece by Piece."
Yeah. I didn't realize.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.234
it was going to --
Yeah, I just --

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:07.968
Look, I was finding a hard time
singing it, like I was like,

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:11.534
I don't know if I want
to really sing that, you know?

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:12.801
And I'm at a different place.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.434
And I was
a very different place, and I.

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.434
-Is it hard for you for have
that happen

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:19.033
in your personal life
when you have the talk show?

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.400
-Yeah.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.234
-You're the most open and
talking every day

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.100
and you're like,
"Well, now I really actually

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.534
have to talk about this
because,

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:26.801
-Yeah, I know.
-...my private life.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.801
-No, totally. And I'm going
to be real with you.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.901
Like, I -- Those were
the last two seasons

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:33.400
specifically were very hard
like behind the scenes.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.934
I don't know
if you've ever done this.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.934
I'm sure you have, because
you've done this for so long.

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.601
But, you know, sometimes you
send your representative

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.334
because it's like,
I can't show up today.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.934
Like I just have to, like,
go through the motions

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:46.367
and be a robot because I, if
I didn't, I would break down.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:49.701
So this is -- I'm excited about
season five here in New York

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:52.067
because it's so -- it's --
I'm in such a great place.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:53.868
My little kids are
in such a great place.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.567
I'm happy, I'm present
in interviews I'm on.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:56.567
-Yes.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.501
It's like, yeah.
Because I wasn't.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:00.868
-I love you, buddy.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.667
I'm here for you
if you need anything.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:04.767
-Thank you.
-But I was thinking about you.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.100
By the way,
congrats on the great reviews

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.000
and success on "Chemistry."
-Thank you.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.133
I saw that you redid
those lyrics and I go,

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:14.367
Oh, my gosh,
that must have been..."

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.734
-But now everybody
wants me to record that one.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.801
[ Laughing ] So, I'm, like...
-That version.

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.133
-The new version
of "Piece by Piece."

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.434
It's like the most requested.
-When I read it,

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.701
somebody wants to do,
it's called the healing version.

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:25.133
-Yeah, it's like a --
But you know what?

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.567
It is very true.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:29.400
Because, you know, now that
I rewrote it literally an hour

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.067
before I went on stage
in Vegas to like,

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:33.434
sing it because I was like,
I can't sing these lyrics,

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:35.501
but I know people want me
to sing the song.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.901
And so I changed it
right before the show,

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:40.934
and, you know, it kind of
put perspective on me as well.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.434
It's like that was a lot
of pressure to put on someone,

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.968
you know, to pick up the pieces
of something of your past.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.334
So it's kind of --
It was a lot of --

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:48.434
There was a lot going on
for me that day,

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:49.467
but it ended up working out.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:50.634
-Do you get emotional
when you...?

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.100
-Do I get emotional
anywhere all the time?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.434
Like, right now?
-Hello, this is my venti.

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:57.434
Hello!
-Welcome to 30 rock!

00:05:57.434 --> 00:06:01.200
-I did not want a venti.
I wanted a large.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.300
This is too much!
Now no one drinks it.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.734
-I just, I don't know
what happened.

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:07.667
It slipped. It slipped.
I don't know what happened.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.200
-Wow.
-It was art.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.834
-I mean,
you're doing this.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.701
I go like, ooph.
I think I would get, like,

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:14.133
all kind of like,

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:15.868
I don't know if I'd make it
through the song.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:17.067
-I don't know, you just do.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.167
-You just do.
-Yeah, you just do.

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:19.501
But yeah,
the audience was really --

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:20.868
My audience is cool.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:22.467
And they were like, cheering me
on because they noticed,

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:24.067
obviously, I started
changing them.

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:25.334
They're very intimate shows.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:26.634
And so these are like fans
that have been with me

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.167
for the ride and they notice

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.701
and then they're all like
screaming, like I'm like,

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:32.934
"Rudy," you know, at the end
of the movie, like making it.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.000
You made it!
-Carrying on their shoulders,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.267
like, "Yeah, Kelly!"

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:37.501
-She's making it.
-She did it.

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.467
-It's -- "Chemistry"
is the name of the album.

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:40.834
I love the title.

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:42.400
Did you always know
that was going to be your title?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.734
-You know,
at once I wrote that song.

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:47.501
I kind of envisioned
it as the title for it,

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:50.234
just because it's definitely
a roller coaster.

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.434
It's not just a divorce album,
it's a relationship album.

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:54.200
There's the good
and the the bad and the hard.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.200
All of it is in there.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.167
So chemistry
can be good and bad.

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.901
-Yeah.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:01.367
-As I've personally
found out as well.

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:03.000
So yeah,
I kind of knew that.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.634
-I love you have a couple
of guest stars

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:07.934
on this album.

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:09.834
-Can you believe it?
Sheila E. is playing on --

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:11.634
That's right.
-Sheila E. is my...

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:12.667
-I love her.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.734
-She's been here
and she can play.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.834
-And she's also
such a quality human.

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:20.100
Like she's so nice.
I love her so much.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.501
And then I asked Steve Martin
because I knew he played banjo

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:25.834
and I referenced the movie
"It's Complicated,"

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:27.267
which is one
of my favorite movies,

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.267
and I've seen it
a billion times,

00:07:29.267 --> 00:07:30.801
and I love him so much.

00:07:30.801 --> 00:07:32.267
And I asked
if he would play on it,

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:35.601
and I totally thought he was
going to say no, and he didn't.

00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:37.934
Yeah. So he's on my record.
-Wait a minute. That's your --

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:39.367
-That's your --
That's your guest stars

00:07:39.367 --> 00:07:41.000
Sheila E. and Steve Martin.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.000
-Who am I?

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.767
-Yeah I was like,
"I have made it."

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:48.133
-Yeah I'm happy that the new
season "Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:49.634
is back, It's on Monday.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:51.067
And I thank you
for being here.

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:52.901
And you're going to perform
for us tonight

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:56.300
I think it's actually...

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.934
But before you're doing
a special performance

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:00.567
tomorrow night.

